Eden uses __ANDROID__ to mean "the Android app" (JNI, content URIs, Logcat,
ADPF, adrenotools, ...). Termux is bionic but builds the Linux desktop (Qt)
frontend, so switch Eden's own app checks to a private macro that is never
defined. The real __ANDROID__ stays defined for bionic-level checks, which are
left untouched on purpose:
  - src/common/host_memory.cpp   (memfd_create syscall fallback, API < 30)
  - src/common/zbic_compression.cpp (no qsort_r in bionic)
  - dynarmic decoder_detail.h    (NDK workaround)
and for third-party code (zstd, Boost.Asio, VMA, ...).

